---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---
<Layout title="Lab" description="Reusable 3D structures and simulations used across the Advanced Biology units.">
  <section class="masthead">
    <p class="k k-c">Lab</p>
    <h1>Structures and simulations</h1>
    <p class="lede">Models built once and used wherever a unit needs them. Everything here runs on the device, offline, with a finger or a mouse.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="ledger-head"><span class="k">Available now</span></div>
  <ul class="doc-grid" style="margin-top: var(--s4)">
    <li>
      <a class="doc link" href={url('/lab/carbon-allotropes/')}>
        <img class="doc-fig" src={url('/lab/carbon/c60.webp')} alt="" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <span class="k k-c">Structure · six models</span>
        <h2>Carbon allotropes</h2>
        <p>Diamond, graphite, graphene, C60, a (10,0) nanotube, and amorphous carbon from published geometry, with a six step walkthrough.</p>
        <span class="action">Open</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note">The water, macromolecule, membrane, and enzyme models arrive with their units.</p>
</Layout>
